# process.nextTick(one, { go: first }); process.nextTick(two, { go: second }); function one(x) { x.go() } function two(x) { x.go() }
# A row of process.nextTick says that the export `nextTick` of internal/process/next_tick_queue is the value of the entry, and the module declares a function under that name.
# One body runs for all callers, where every callback would meet every argument. So no operand goes into it: the overloads of the entry are applied with the operands of each call,
# and each callback gets what was passed with it.
